Verse 1:
[F]O Jesus, I have prom[C]ised To [C7]serve Thee to the [F]end;
[F]Be [D7]Thou forever near [Gm]me, My [G]Master and my [C]Friend;
[E]I [F]shall not fear the bat[C]tle If [C7]Thou art by my [F]side,
Nor [D7]wander from the path[Gm]way If [F]Thou wilt [C7]be my [F]Guide.

Verse 2:
[F]O [C]let me [C7]feel thee [F]near me!
[F]The [D7]world [Gm]is [G]ever [C]near;
[E]I [F]see [C]the [C7]sights [F]that dazzle,
[D7]the [Gm]tempting [F]sounds [C7]I [F]hear;
[F]my [C]foes are [C7]ever [F]near me,
[F][D7]around [Gm]me [G]and [C]within;
[E]but [F]Jesus, [C]draw [C7]thou [F]nearer,
[D7]and [Gm]shield [F]my [C7]soul [F]from sin.

Verse 3:
[F]O [C]Jesus, [C7]thou [F]hast promised
[F]to [D7]all [Gm]who [G]follow [C]thee
[E]that [F]where [C]thou [C7]art [F]in glory
[D7]there [Gm]shall [F]thy [C7]servant [F]be.
[F]And [C]Jesus, [C7]I [F]have promised
[F]to [D7]serve [Gm]thee [G]to [C]the end;
[E]O [F]give [C]me [C7]grace [F]to follow,
[D7]my [Gm]Master [F]and [C7]my [F]Friend.
